# Wayfinder environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every one of these is OPTIONAL — with none set,
# the app runs in local (device-only) mode and never makes network calls.

# ── Backend: pooled navigation signals + search misses + shared venues (Railway Postgres) ──
# Railway's Postgres plugin exposes two connection strings. The app reads either.
#   • On Railway: DATABASE_URL (the private …​.railway.internal host).
#   • On Vercel (or anywhere reaching Railway over the internet): DATABASE_PUBLIC_URL.
# Set whichever matches where the app runs. TLS is turned on automatically for a
# remote host, so ?sslmode=require is not required in the string.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_PUBLIC_URL=

# ── AI sign-reading in Survey Mode (server-side only) ────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Real outdoor routing + place search (server-side only) ───────────────────
MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Optional accounts (Clerk) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in is deliberately optional and additive. Wayfinder works fully
# anonymously — you never have to sign in to find a ward, the same way Google
# Maps and Apple Maps let you navigate signed out. An account only carries the
# things that must follow a *person* rather than a device: saved places, and
# ownership of a venue you mapped.
#
# With these unset, ClerkProvider is not mounted (src/app/layout.tsx) and
# src/proxy.ts is a pass-through, so the app behaves exactly as it always has.
#
# Note src/proxy.ts deliberately EXCLUDES /navigate from the auth matcher: that
# is the route used inside hospitals where signal dies, and it must never depend
# on an auth round-trip.
#
# Keys: https://dashboard.clerk.com/ → your app → API keys
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# ── The back office at /backoffice (see docs/back-office.md) ──────────────────────
# The ONE part of this app that inverts the "no key → feature quietly off" rule
# above. Every other integration failing soft is right; a back office failing
# soft would be an open door onto every shared venue, every trail and every
# delete button. So with neither variable below set, /backoffice authorises nobody
# and shows setup instructions instead.
#
# Set EITHER of these. Both may be set at once; either is sufficient.
#
# 1. Clerk accounts on an allowlist — preferred where Clerk is configured, since
#    the audit log then names a person rather than "the shared password", and
#    sign-in inherits whatever the organisation already enforces.
ADMIN_EMAILS=
#
# 2. A shared password, exchanged for a signed 12-hour session cookie. For
#    deployments running without accounts, and for getting the first operator in.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
#
# Optional. Signs the session cookie. Without it the signing key is derived from
# ADMIN_PASSWORD, which means changing the password ends every open session —
# usually what you want, occasionally not.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Venue moderation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POST /api/venues needs no account: that is what lets someone map their own
# department in ten minutes, and it means anything anyone types is offered to
# every user in the picker. Set this to `queue` to hold each new venue until an
# administrator lists it in the back office. Unset (the default) keeps the
# original behaviour — venues are listed immediately and reviewed afterwards.
WAYFINDER_VENUE_MODERATION=
